<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Supreme Council of the Republic of Latvia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1990–1993</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Supreme Council of Latvia was the parliament elected in March 1990, in which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/popular-front-of-latvia">Popular Front of Latvia</a> won a majority. On 4 May 1990, under its chairman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolijs-gorbunovs">Anatolijs Gorbunovs</a>, it declared the restoration of Latvia's independence with a transition period, completed on 21 August 1991. It governed until the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saeima">Saeima</a> was elected in 1993.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/supreme-council-of-the-republic-of-latvia.jpg" alt="Supreme Council of the Republic of Latvia" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Zscout370 at English Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Latvia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
